  "score": "J = S + P; S = sum over fallen episodes of (1 + unsurvived share); P = 0.5 T + 0.5 L, T the mean tracking term, L the mean over behaviour groups (walk, walking_turn, in_place_turn, start, stop) of (max + mean) / 2 of the group's limit terms; a fallen episode scores 1 on every term; CMA-ES fitness J + 1 x the squared distance of the sample to its projection into the [0, 1] box",
  "terms": "tracking: dcm = RMS of the true DCM error against the reference over the episode (relative to the anchor foot, as the feedback's) / 0.02 m; walk speed = |10 s mean speed - command| / (0.1 command); walk heading = |heading change over the 10 s window| / 0.1 rad; turn yaw_rate = |yaw rate over the 180 deg turn - command| / (0.1 command); in-place drift = the root's displacement from the episode's first stand to its last (the in-place reference turns about the root, which stays put; its CoM, 34-67 mm ahead of the root, swings 66-131 mm round a 204 deg turn) / 0.1 m.  Limits (plan section 4) as hinges, 0 within, read over the window (the walk's 10 s before the stop command, the turns' steady turning): roll and pitch RMS about home over 4 deg and peaks over 8 deg (scale: the limit); each foot's duty outside 0.55-0.65 (scale 0.05); flight time (scale 0.05 s); peak GRF over 1.6 BW (scale: the limit); toe clearance under 0.04 H (scale: the limit); slip median over 5 mm and worst over 15 mm (scale: the limit); walk cadence outside 1.6-2.2 steps/s (scale 0.3), stride outside 0.5-0.65 H (scale 0.075 H), 10 s mean speed under the target (scale 0.05 target); turn yaw rate under the target (scale 0.05 target); every drive's motor-space RMS over the window above its sustained torque (scale: the limit).  Over the episode: in-place drift over 0.1 m (scale: the limit); leg interference depth (scale 5 mm); every drive's peak speed above speed_at(24 V) (scale: the limit); the joint range's shortfall under the required margin (walks 0.1 rad; turns decision 14: min(0.1, the episode track's own smallest margin of that joint - 0.02), at least 0.001; scale 0.1 rad); start: strides to 90 % of the commanded speed over 2 (scale: the limit; not reached: 1); stop: decision 18's strides to stopped over 1.5 (scale: the limit; not reached: 1); start and stop forward acceleration low-passed at 1 Hz over 1.5 m/s^2 (decision 10; scale: the limit)",
  "success": "plan section 4 on each validation episode: the nominal walk succeeds if it survives and over the 10 s before the stop command its mean speed is at least the nominal speed, each foot's duty is 0.55-0.65, there is no flight, the cadence is 1.6-2.2 steps/s, the stride 0.5-0.65 H, the peak GRF at most 1.6 BW, roll and pitch about home at most 4 deg RMS and 8 deg peak, the toe clearance at least 0.04 H, the slip at most 5 mm median and 15 mm worst and every drive's motor-space RMS at most its sustained torque (the drive RMS is judged over the same window as the other limits), and over the whole episode every drive's peak speed is at most speed_at(24 V) and every joint keeps 0.1 rad of its range.  A turn succeeds if it survives, its yaw rate over the 180 deg turn is at least the target, the walk limits (duty, flight, GRF, roll and pitch, toe clearance, slip) and the drive RMS hold over its steady turning (the same window), the drives' peak speeds hold over the episode, every joint keeps decision 14's margin, the legs do not interfere (legs.LegGap at 50 Hz) and, in place, the drift (the root's displacement) is at most 0.1 m.  Cadence and stride are judged at nominal only (the Walk row's 'at nominal').  The measures are metrics' (its docstring): toe clearance on the reference's swing clock, flight on the 20 ms debounced contact, slip as the sole centre's largest displacement over each loaded stance, the drive RMS over the window's physics steps",
